[0.136,"o","\u001b[H\r\u001b[6B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mPlease implement this issue.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m#45 Count overdue days in business days\u001b[39m                                                 \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mAccounting counts how long an invoice is overdue in business days, and the aging report\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mshould too: weekends and public holidays don't count. An invoice due on a Friday is 1 \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mbusiness day overdue on the next Monday.\u001b[39m                                                \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mThe holidays change every year, so keep them in a JSON file that accounting can update \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mwithout touching the code. The list for 2026: 2026-01-01, 2026-01-19, 2026-02-16, \u001b[39m      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m2026-05-25, 2026-06-19, 2026-07-03, 2026-09-07, 2026-10-12, 2026-11-11, 2026-11-26, \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m2026-12-25.\u001b[39m                                                                             \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mThe accountant runs invoicer from the package (see the README), so it has to work \u001b[39m      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mthere.\u001b[39m                                                                                  \r\u001b[8B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;174m✻\u001b[3GM\u001b[38;5;216mist\u001b[38;5;174ming… \r\u001b[3B\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m